  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Initially electrophilic addition reaction takes place and form alcohol and alkyl bromide. Then Wurtz reaction takes place.</p><p>The Wurtz reaction is a very useful reaction in the fields of organic chemistry and organometallic chemistry for the formation of alkanes. In this reaction, two different alkyl halides are coupled to yield a longer alkane&nbsp;chain with the help of sodium and dry ether solution.</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0106_cb020a04b04f.jpeg\" /><img src=\"assets\\st0106_6321849475d1.jpeg\" /></p>"
